Fix waliter.test on systems with 64KB pages

Each shm mapping covers a whole number of system pages (see
unixShmRegionPerMap() in os_unix.c), so with 64KB pages the shm file of
the 10000 frame WAL in test 1.2 is rounded up from three to four 32KB
regions.  Derive the expected file size from the system page size
instead of hard-coding three regions.

--- a/test/waliter.test
+++ b/test/waliter.test
@@ -65,9 +65,16 @@
   UPDATE t1 SET b = randomblob(900);
 } {0}
 
+# Each shm mapping covers a whole number of system pages, so the number of
+# 32KB shm regions is rounded up to a multiple of the number of regions per
+# page.  This matters with 64KB pages, where it is two.
+if {[catch {exec getconf PAGESIZE} pgsz]} { set pgsz 4096 }
+set nShmPerMap [expr {$pgsz>32768 ? $pgsz/32768 : 1}]
+set nShmRegion [expr {(3 + $nShmPerMap - 1) / $nShmPerMap * $nShmPerMap}]
+
 do_test 1.2 {
   file size test.db-shm
-} [expr 32768 * 3]
+} [expr 32768 * $nShmRegion]
 
 do_execsql_test 1.3 {
   PRAGMA wal_checkpoint
